# Blog posts are .mdx by extension and plain HTML by content — `lib/blog-data.ts`
# reads the body after the frontmatter and the page renders it with
# dangerouslySetInnerHTML. There is no MDX compiler in this project: no
# @mdx-js, no remark, no rehype.
#
# Prettier does not know that. It parses .mdx as MDX/JSX, and on 2026-04 it
# rewrote 26 files "that had drifted" (#18) — inserting 42 `{" "}` JSX whitespace
# expressions as line-wrap separators and reflowing the contents of multi-line
# <pre><code> blocks.
#
# In MDX both are correct. Here, nothing evaluates them: `{" "}` shipped as six
# literal characters in the middle of a sentence, and the reflowed code samples
# rendered word-wrapped inside a <pre>, which preserves whitespace — one of them
# pulled three statements onto a line that began with `//`, commenting them out.
# All of it was live on the three flagship engineering posts until 2026-09-20.
#
# Removing the tokens by hand is not a fix: `prettier --write .` puts all 42 back
# (verified). The formatter has to stop reading these files at all.
content/blog/
